<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The `curia-mcp` command: the MCP adapter of §11.5, as R11.16 (revised) permits it — a driving
    adapter over the application layer that serves the HTTP API, reaching that layer across the
    network rather than in process. It runs on the agent operator's host, speaks MCP over stdio to
    the consuming model, and reaches the Forum through Curia.Client over HTTPS.

    Why agent-side and not beside Curia.Api: R11.20 forbids the MCP server holding agent private
    keys where the deployment allows separation, which only reduces risk where the process belongs
    to the agent's operator; and R11.17's `curia_verify` verifies "locally", which Forum-side would
    mean the Forum confirming its own signature. Entry G11 carries the argument.

    The reference to Curia.Client is the second from src/ — Curia.Client.Cli is the first — and
    carries the same consequence: everything this host does is a call into that library, so the
    guarantees are the library's rather than this project's. R11.16 (revised) forbids this adapter
    deciding a question the application layer decides, and having no path to the domain except
    through the client is how that is kept true by construction rather than by review.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Curia.Mcp</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>curia-mcp</AssemblyName>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="ModelContextProtocol.Core" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Curia.Client/Curia.Client.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
